{"lines": ["On Wednesday, the sixth of April, 1966, students and a teacher at Westall High School, in Melbourne, Australia, reported a flying object.", "It was described as round, with a domed top, white, grey, or silver. Some said it descended behind a row of trees into an open area called the Grange.", "Some accounts had it pursued by five aircraft. Others said it hovered instead of landing.", "Afterward, students described a circle of grass as burnt, boiled, or pressed down. The numbers of circles varied from one to three.", "On the ninth of April, air force personnel and UFO enthusiasts visited the field and reported nothing of interest.", "A Melbourne newspaper suggested a weather balloon. Researcher Keith Basterfield later found documents suggesting a high-altitude test balloon, launched from Mildura, may have blown off course and come down near the school.", "A skeptic, Brian Dunning, warned that over the years, descriptions had become diluted with details from people who may not have seen anything.", "That is why you record each account separately, before the stories blend together."], "words": [["On", 0.0, 0.14], ["Wednesday,", 0.14, 0.38], ["the", 0.74, 0.92], ["sixth", 0.92, 1.42], ["of", 1.42, 1.47], ["April,", 1.47, 1.76], ["1966,", 1.76, 3.02], ["students", 3.76, 4.1], ["and", 4.1, 4.58], ["a", 4.58, 4.7], ["teacher", 4.7, 5.0], ["at", 5.0, 5.42], ["Westall", 5.42, 5.92], ["High", 5.92, 6.14], ["School,", 6.14, 6.54], ["in", 6.54, 6.92], ["Melbourne,", 6.92, 7.18], ["Australia,", 7.58, 8.06], ["reported", 8.66, 8.96], ["a", 8.96, 9.28], ["flying", 9.28, 9.62], ["object.", 9.62, 10.14], ["It", 11.2, 11.32], ["was", 11.32, 11.46], ["described", 11.46, 11.88], ["as", 11.88, 12.36], ["round,", 12.36, 12.7], ["with", 12.7, 13.12], ["a", 13.12, 13.24], ["domed", 13.24, 13.8], ["top,", 13.8, 14.08], ["white,", 14.38, 14.64], ["grey,", 14.64, 15.16], ["or", 15.16, 15.68], ["silver.", 15.68, 15.98], ["Some", 16.82, 16.98], ["said", 16.98, 17.32], ["it", 17.32, 